  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>The University of Notre Dame Australia (UNDA) is a private Catholic university established in 1989. Unlike large public universities, UNDA is known for its small class sizes and personalised teaching.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>Student life at the University of Notre Dame is welcoming, as you’ll find clubs and societies for various interests. Beyond academics, the university offers career development, employability services, and counselling support.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>The university offers various accommodation options near campus. Most residences are only a 10–15 minute walk away.</p><p style=\"text-align:center;\"><i>If you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to </i><a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\"><i>download our app</i></a><i> and check out the Stays feature!</i></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Library</strong><br>You’ll have access to a well-resourced library with study spaces and research support.</p><p><strong>Sports</strong><br>On campus, you’ll find fitness centres, along with university sports clubs and teams.</p><p><strong>Laboratory</strong><br>You’ll find many top-notch labs, research areas, and learning centres across the campuses.<br>&nbsp;</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
